messages:
maya (DevEx): Quick heads-up — found multiple README snippets in /examples/chat that are copy/paste broken after the JS SDK rename + auth var change. @phil can you take a look?
phil: thanks. can you paste the exact failing snippet?
maya (DevEx): sure — current README has this (copied from master):
```js
const Redwood = require('redwood-js-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.OLD_API_KEY });

const res = await client.generate('Hello');
```
maya (DevEx): node throws `TypeError: client.generate is not a function` because the new SDK surface moved to `chat.generate` and the package is now `@redwood/inference-js`.
jen (SDK): omg yeah — we renamed package + split APIs. also env var is now `RW_API_KEY` not `OLD_API_KEY` which people keep copy/pasting.
phil: also noticed retry defaults changed in v0.9 — README still says "retries: 3". SDK default is 0 which explains a bunch of transient 429 errors folks reported. we should call that out.
maya (DevEx): opened PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/789 that updates examples, fixes auth var names, and adds a migration note. added a before/after snippet in the README: 
```js
// before (broken)
const Redwood = require('redwood-js-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.OLD_API_KEY });
await client.generate('Hi');

// after (working)
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference-js');
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY, retry: { maxRetries: 3 } });
await client.chat.generate({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hi' }] });
```
docs-bot: PR opened by maya: "docs: update examples + migration note" — https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/789
phil: can we also add a short warning about leaving placeholder keys like `REDACTED_API_KEY` in examples? we've had at least two incidents where people deployed with the placeholder.
jen (SDK): good call. I'll add a tiny paragraph and a CI smoke test that runs the node examples to catch runtime failures.
maya (DevEx): added `npm run examples:smoke` to the GH actions workflow in the PR. linking: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/789/files
deploy-bot: CI queued: examples-smoke (branch: docs/update-examples)
deploy-bot: CI passed: examples-smoke (run 452) — node examples executed against staging fixture
phil: sweet. after merge we should cherry-pick into the release branch and add a short blurb in the changelog about SDK rename + auth var rename.
maya (DevEx): PR merged and cherry-picked to `release/v0.9.x`. closing the loop. thanks everyone :party_parrot:
phil: thanks for driving this. helps onboarding a lot — tiny copy/paste issues are the worst UX.
jen (SDK): agreed. I'll follow up with a small SDK patch to detect old env var names and emit a helpful error message to users.
maya (DevEx): perfect. closing thread.
